# elizaOS App vendors a content-pinned Node.js runtime and its production
# npm dependency closure under /usr/lib/elizaos-app. The tags below are
# structural consequences of that reviewed, provenance-pinned vendoring —
# not packaging accidents — and each is intentionally accepted:
#
# The upstream Node.js distribution statically embeds zlib/openssl/etc. and
# is shipped byte-for-byte to preserve its published sha256 provenance.
elizaos-app: embedded-library
elizaos-app: statically-linked-binary
# Stripping or rewriting the audited binaries would break the recorded
# executable digests (see elizaos-runtime-provenance.json).
elizaos-app: unstripped-binary-or-object
elizaos-app: no-code-sections
# Interpreter scripts inside the vendored tree (npm's own bin shims, dep
# tooling) run against the bundled Node runtime on PATH, never the host's;
# the wrapper prepends /usr/lib/elizaos-app/node/bin.
elizaos-app: missing-dep-for-interpreter
# Dependency tarballs ship developer-tooling residue (declared license
# terms are retained separately in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.json).
elizaos-app: package-contains-eslint-config-file
elizaos-app: package-contains-npm-ignore-file
# Bundled dependency docs/templates reference external assets; nothing in
# the runtime fetches them (they are inert files inside node_modules).
elizaos-app: privacy-breach-facebook
elizaos-app: privacy-breach-logo
elizaos-app: privacy-breach-uses-embedded-file
# Helper scripts inside vendored deps (e.g. gyp) declare python shebangs;
# they are build-time helpers that the packaged runtime never executes.
elizaos-app: python3-script-but-no-python3-dep
